WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.168
-And congratulations,
by the way,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.235
on a great first
season with the Pistons.

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.637
-Thank you.
-You did a great job.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.072
You went all the way
to the playoffs.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.074
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, thank you.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.843
-How is your off-season going?
-It's been good.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.011
-Yeah.
-Just hanging out,

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.412
enjoying some time off.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.181
-What do you think about this
whole deal -- free agency?

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.617
That went kind of crazy.
-It is.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.218
But honestly, man --
-With the Nets and Clippers.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.187
-Almost everybody.
-Did you know about --

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.357
Do people know about this stuff
before it hits the news or...?

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.526
-I feel like -- I mean,
I find out about

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.127
some of the stuff just as a fan.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.096
-You didn't know
about any of these --

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.297
-Some of the guys
you kind of know.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.599
You kind of hear some things.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:34.834
But I was at the comedy store
the other night.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.569
And when Kawhi
went to the Clippers --

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.670
-Yeah.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.071
-My friend was onstage
doing a set.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.240
And I was like -- it started
happening, like, rolling in.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.508
He came off.
He was like, "How was it?"

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.744
I was like, "I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.645
This is huge."
-"I'm on Twitter right now.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:47.947
This is giant." Yeah.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.549
That's how you found out
is on Twitter?

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.717
-Yeah.
-Wow. That's --

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.518
-Just like everybody else.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.021
But you -- you also love comedy.
I love that you love comedy.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:58.057
What got you into comedy?
-I think just, you know,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.393
from an early age watching
comedy with my dad,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.095
"Saturday Night Live."
And then --

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.363
-Who were some of your
favorites?

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.098
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.799
-[ Clears throat ]

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.702
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:13.072
-On "Saturday Night Live?"
-Yeah.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.874
-Well, I mean, obviously,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.043
you have to mention, um...

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.845
like, Adam Sandler.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.247
[ Laughter ]
-You were really great.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.116
-Oh, thank you so much!
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.984
You didn't have to say that.
You didn't have to say it!

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.320
[ Cheers and applause ]
You didn't have to that at all.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.856
Oh, my gosh! What are your
favorite characters of mine?

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:33.192
[ Laughter ]
No, no.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:36.095
But then you started
doing stand-up yourself?

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.397
-I did, man.
I kind of stumbled into it.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.499
I was going to go to
"Just for Laughs" in Montreal.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:41.534
-I love "Just for Laughs."

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.968
-This was four years ago,
I think.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.870
And I had a call
with the director.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.039
And he was like,
"You know, we should find

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.340
something fun for you to do."
And he was like,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.841
"Do you want to host
the 'Midnight Surprise Show'"?

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.309
I was like, "Yeah, sure."

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.645
Thinking I was just going to be
like, "And now, so-and-so."

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.013
-Yeah.
-And it turned out

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.381
I had to do like ten minutes.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.151
So I had to go write
ten minutes. And --

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:01.020
-What did you write about?
-Just basketball, you know.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.721
[ Laughter ]
The only thing I know, man.

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:04.490
-Do what you know, man. Yeah.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.858
And it worked out.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:09.895
And now I've written
a whole new 15 minutes or so.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.397
And I've been --
I worked on it in L.A.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.765
I'm going to go out tonight.
And --

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.700
-That's fun.
-Yeah, we'll see how it goes.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.869
-And so this thing is July 25th,
I believe.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:20.540
If you go to the website,
hahaha.com.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.740
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.342
I can't believe they got that
website.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.977
-Three "has", yeah.
-Three "has" and go

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.046
"Comedy By Blake."
Get tickets to go see this.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.181
Have you ever been heckled?

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:31.383
-Not while I was doing comedy.

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:33.185
I get heckled all the time
playing basketball.

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:35.087
[ Laughter ]
-Just by fans yelling?

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.589
-Yeah, just fans.
Especially on the road.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.125
There was a guy one time, like,
one of my very first games

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.727
in Portland.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.395
I was a rookie, just checked in.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.864
And this guy named Kurt Thomas
was standing next to me.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.399
-Sure.
-And it got so quiet

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.735
in the arena, so everybody
can hear this guy.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:51.170
And he goes, "Hey, Blake,
the coolest thing

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.439
you've ever done is stand next
to Kurt Thomas."

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.608
[ Laughter ]
I was like --

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.443
-That's pretty good.
-Yeah, I mean, at this point,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.811
yeah.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.279
He's right, yeah. Absolutely.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:03.683
Has it helped your basketball
at all, doing standup?

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.118
-Not really the physical part
of basketball.

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:08.387
[ Laughter ]
But definitely -- you know,

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.590
like, after the game,
you have to do media.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.092
And you have to sit at a press
conference and answer questions.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.327
And I feel like people
always think athletes

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:17.664
are really stupid.
And it's not that we're stupid.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:20.232
It's just that we've just
exercised for two hours.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:23.035
And there's not really enough
oxygen in our brains to --

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:25.204
[ Laughter ]
-To answer tricky questions.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.239
-To actually be able to --
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.574
-Yeah.
-I mean, can I show you?

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.376
-Sure.
-All right, stand up for me.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.244
-Okay.
-You need just a little space.

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:33.412
Do you want to come here?
-Sure.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.215
-All right. So what I want you
to do --

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.616
-Okay.
-Run in place, jumping jacks,

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:38.517
whatever you want.
-Okay.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.452
-For 15 seconds. And then,

00:03:40.452 --> 00:03:42.388
as soon as you're done, I'm just
going to ask you some questions.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.457
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.992
-I see where this is going.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.027
-While you're doing it,
I'm going to commentate

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.161
on how you're doing it.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.963
-Oh, my -- this is the --

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:52.031
♪♪

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.166
-All right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:56.369
Start off really slow.
All right.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.972
Quick feet, by the way.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.774
And stop. All right, Jimmy.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.042
-Yeah.
-Tell me how you're feeling?

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.377
Tell me about how you're feeling
about how you feel.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.678
-I just --
-All right.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.614
[ Laughter ]
And, one more time,

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.316
how did you feel when you
first started out there?

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.684
-I don't --
-See how stupid that sounds?

00:04:12.684 --> 00:04:14.554
[ Laughter ]
It's not --

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.889
It's not our fault.
-It's not your fault.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.090
It's not your fault.
-It's not our fault.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.391
-Blake Griffin, everybody.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:23.563
Go to hahaha.com for tickets
to "Comedy By Blake."

